+The known lower coefficients were never used to calibrate the estimator.
+Half-run splits, the two different ordering maps, and the change of bit
+resolution are additional diagnostics.  The per-replicate influence
+records also expose whether a single rare sample batch dominates an
+estimated variance; no outlying replicate is discarded.
+
+The nonlinear fixed-point map has a small finite-sample bias.  A
+leave-one-replicate-out calculation estimates its leading effect;
+the central estimate remains the direct pooled estimator, rather than
+silently applying a data-dependent correction.  A separate finite
+Lagrange expansion checks the same input jets, and a replicate bootstrap
+checks variance propagation.  Bootstrap intervals in the records are
+approximate diagnostics, not rigorous error certificates.  The common
+$K_{76}$ uncertainty is varied once per complete bootstrap sample.  For
+this diagnostic it is modeled by one normal draw with its recorded
+variance; this modeling choice is not a proof that the retained input
+error is normally distributed.  The reported covariance formula itself
+uses only that variance.
