+\subsection{Arithmetic, checks and reproducibility}
+For cancellation monitoring, the original long-double kernel evaluation
+is repeated in binary128 when its signed sum is small compared with the
+sum of absolute terms.  Extremely severe cancellation invokes a
+300-decimal-digit emergency branch.  All fallback counts are recorded,
+and no nonfinite sampled point is accepted.
+
+The independently constructed reference uses Kirchhoff cofactor
+\emph{determinants}, not the sampler's list of spanning-tree monomials.
+There are 1,038 successful kernel comparisons over dimensions 2 and 3,
+including all finite kernels and endpoint configurations extending to
+$10^{-130}$.  Ordinary points use 70 reference digits and extreme points
+use 650.  The 70-digit Gamma-jet checks and the exact rational ordering
+checks are separate tests.  These validate the changed integration
+implementation, not all preceding field-theory reductions.
+
+An optional guarded-double path was tested on exactly the same pilot
+samples and compared against the original path.  Its differences in the
+assembled $C_6$ were negligible at the new sampling scale.  Production
+nevertheless uses the original long-double entry path in both campaigns;
+the optional performance experiment is not part of the estimator.
+
+The accompanying archive contains each raw production replicate and its
+individual graph contributions, frozen graph allocations, randomization
+seeds and direction matrices, two-loop and known-sector inputs, the
+retained power-audit records, the kernel source and independent check
+scripts.  From the archive root the primary commands are
+\begin{lstlisting}[language=bash]
+python code/final_analysis.py
+python code/extra_checks.py
+python code/check_structure.py
+sh code/build.sh
+python code/check_kernels.py
+\end{lstlisting}
+The first command recomputes both full coefficients and their covariance
+without running an expensive integration.  New samples can be generated
+with a new tag using \texttt{code/run\_precision.py}; existing result files
+are never overwritten.  The exact delivered campaign is specified in
+\texttt{inputs/production\_plan.json}.  The source audit preserves all
+previous displayed mathematical blocks in order.  Earlier error bars
+remain visible as historical results; the present numerical precision
+supersedes them, without changing any analytic coefficient formula.
